    {
      "id": "2114945022756089862",
      "author": "elonmusk",
      "author_name": "Elon Musk",
      "author_avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2053244804520427520/m8mdWZCG_200x200.jpg",
      "author_verified": true,
      "author_verified_type": "individual",
      "created_at_utc": "2026-10-27T04:59:21.000Z",
      "created_at_shanghai": "2026-10-27 12:59:21",
      "type": "转发",
      "type_label": "转发",
      "text": "I see how some people can watch flashy robot demos on the timeline and think with a shiver that the robot apocalypse is around the corner, but reality check:\n\nThere is no robot in the world that can change the batteries in a jack-o-lantern.\n\nIf you have a robot friendly door handle it might be able to walk outside, pick it up, and carry it back inside. The robot could open the drawer with your batteries in it, but then things get tough.\n\nOpening the package of AA batteries?\nExtracting a precision screwdriver from its case?\nUnscrewing four tiny screws that require a hard press and twist?\nPopping batteries out of the case?\n\nYes, you could build and train a specialist robot to do that today, but there is a very long way to go to replace the full range of human capabilities. Near term doomer scenarios should stop at “secretly controlling humanity” instead of “wiping humanity out” 😀",
      "quote": null,
      "retweet": {
        "author": "ID_AA_Carmack",
        "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1560764938083352577/B1X3m4NN_200x200.jpg",
        "created_at_shanghai": "2026-10-27 09:51:36",
        "created_at_utc": "2026-10-27T01:51:36.000Z",
        "id": "2114897771001974921",
        "images": [],
        "media": [],
        "name": "John Carmack",
        "text": "I see how some people can watch flashy robot demos on the timeline and think with a shiver that the robot apocalypse is around the corner, but reality check:\n\nThere is no robot in the world that can change the batteries in a jack-o-lantern.\n\nIf you have a robot friendly door handle it might be able to walk outside, pick it up, and carry it back inside. The robot could open the drawer with your batteries in it, but then things get tough.\n\nOpening the package of AA batteries?\nExtracting a precision screwdriver from its case?\nUnscrewing four tiny screws that require a hard press and twist?\nPopping batteries out of the case?\n\nYes, you could build and train a specialist robot to do that today, but there is a very long way to go to replace the full range of human capabilities. Near term doomer scenarios should stop at “secretly controlling humanity” instead of “wiping humanity out” 😀",
        "url": "https://x.com/ID_AA_Carmack/status/2114897771001974921",
        "verified": true,
        "verified_type": "individual"
      },
