            "width": 2816
          }
        ],
        "name": "Sawyer Merritt",
        "text": "Tesla has released new FSD (Supervised) safety data.\n\nMiles per major collision:\n• Teslas Driven With FSD (Supervised): 6,006,200\n• Teslas Driven Manually (Active Safety Features): 2,031,221\n• Teslas Driven Manually (No Active Safety Features): 845,915\n• U.S. Average: 660,164\n\nTotal major collisions:\n• Teslas with FSD (Supervised): 1,579\n• Teslas driven manually with Active Safety: 17,775\n• Teslas driven manually without Active Safety: 239\n• U.S. average: 4,989,713\n\nTotal miles logged:\n• Teslas with FSD (Supervised): 9,483,790,215\n• Teslas driven manually with Active Safety: 36,104,958,020\n• Teslas driven manually without Active Safety: 202,173,600\n• U.S. drivers overall: 3,294,031,000,000\n\nTesla vehicles with FSD (Supervised) engaged experienced ~9x fewer major collisions than those driving without it on.\n\nThis is North America data across all road classes (highway and non-highway). The data reflects a rolling twelve-month aggregation of miles and collisions.",
        "url": "https://x.com/SawyerMerritt/status/2114924525536034869",
        "verified": true,
        "verified_type": "individual"
      },
